WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:00.567
U.S.

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:01.501
fighter jets being

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.069
scrambled and shooting down

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.038
three mysterious flying objects

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.107
in just the last three days alone.

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.274
The White House and Pentagon

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:08.575
are now

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.743
facing growing pressure

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:10.944
to answer just basic

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:12.512
but burning questions.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.514
What are these objects? Who sent them?

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.583
They were all different shapes and sizes.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.450
According to officials.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.452
They were flying at different altitudes.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:20.820
We're told that the latest object

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.254
was shaped

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.255
like an octagon

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.024
and shot down over Michigan near

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:24.958
Lake Huron.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.192
It was only flying 20,000

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.194
feet up much lower than the objects

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:28.628
that were

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:29.496
shot down over

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:31.197
Alaska and Canada on Friday

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.799
and Saturday, respectively.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.467
It was at a lower than cruising

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.335
the cruising altitude

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.936
of a commercial airliner.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.638
The suspected Chinese spy balloon

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.272
that flew across

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.508
the US was 60,000 feet in the air

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:42.342
for comparison's,

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:42.642
a lot

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.511
higher than the other objects

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.379
we've been seeing in recent days.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.847
But lawmakers from both sides of

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:48.982
the aisle are demanding

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.884
more details from the White House,

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.352
including the Republican chair

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.887
of the House Intelligence Committee,

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.155
Mike Turner.

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:57.257
They prefer them to be trigger happy

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:58.691
than to be permissive.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:00:59.759
But we're going to have to see

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:00.260
whether or not

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.328
this is just the administration trying to

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.763
to change headlines.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.131
What we're seeing here

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.866
is a number of announcements

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:07.867
by the administration

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.235
without any real information

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.503
being given to Congress.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:11.638
This could be because they

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:13.106
don't have any information.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.475
Our national security correspondent

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.010
Kelly Ayotte is at the State Department.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.378
And I think that's a good question.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:19.345
What do they know?

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.146
Do they know something

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.581
that they're holding back or is it

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:22.882
they're not saying a lot publicly

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.218
because they don't really know a lot.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.252
Caitlin, it's pretty clear

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.587
that they just don't know a lot

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:28.021
right now.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.323
We spoke with some Pentagon officials

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.591
on the phone last night,

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.492
and they put it

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.527
pretty blatantly when they said

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.061
one of them

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.129
that they believe

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.664
that this is the first time

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:38.598
that US Northern

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.801
Command has used kinetic action,

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:42.769
the military,

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:45.405
to take down an airborne object in U.S.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:45.972
airspace.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:48.007
So this is pretty unimpressive dented.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.442
They are still trying to figure out

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.610
a lot of the questions

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.412
that lawmakers have answers to now

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.246
over the weekend.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.114
President Biden

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.949
spoke with Prime Minister

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.784
Justin Trudeau of Canada

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.352
and they spoke after that

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.020
object was downed over Canada.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.455
They both authorized

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.723
the downing of that object.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:04.991
What they focused on

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.726
was the need for recovery

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.228
to a better understand

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.062
the origin

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.964
and the purpose of that object.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.265
But as you noted,

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.700
just out of the front there,

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:14.901
there were three objects

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.803
that were downed over the course of three

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.137
days.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:18.104
On Friday,

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.806
there was an object downed over US

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.674
coastal waters around Alaska,

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.843
then the one over Canada on Saturday.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:26.446
On Sunday, another object down by U.S.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:28.781
fighter jets over Lake Huron.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.450
Now, there is no clear connection

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.618
to any of these.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:32.986
And that Chinese spy balloon

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.320
that was down off the coast

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.556
of South Carolina just last weekend.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.691
But the recovery efforts here are

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:39.592
what U.S.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.027
officials are really looking

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:42.662
at to try and learn more

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.864
about where these objects came from,

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.367
what they were doing in U.S. airspace.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.835
And we heard last night

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:49.536
from the commander

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.104
of Northern Command, however,

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.139
that recovery efforts for that object

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.741
that was down over the coastal waters

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:56.743
around Alaska hasn't even begun.

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.311
Because the teams are still working

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.413
to locate that object.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.614
Yeah, we'll see what happens

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:02.949
when they do finally located.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.317
Kylie Atwood, thank you.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:05.218
There's lots to discuss now.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.419
Joining us now, CNN political

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.187
and national security

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:09.222
analyst David Sanger and retired U.S.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.257
Army Major Mike Lyons.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.258
Good to see both of you.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.259
Thank you very much.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.128
So I'm interested in what you have to say

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:15.628
about this.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:16.196
Mike Lyons,

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:17.697
because you are saying that

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.832
this is a wake up call.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.767
What why do you say

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:21.701
this is a wake up call?

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:22.502
No, I think it is.

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:23.269
It puts

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.637
the United States on notice

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.006
for this great power competition

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:27.974
between us and China.

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:30.109
This one at 60,000 feet potentially.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.878
This is high altitude

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:32.478
airspace

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.513
that in the past

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.180
that the Chinese

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.249
have encroached on before

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.817
in other nations as well.

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.052
And we've just kind of ignored it.

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.253
And now

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:41.521
we're going to have to put the resources

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:42.956
towards looking over the horizon,

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.290
especially in areas

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.625
in the north in Alaska,

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:46.426
so to speak,

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:48.127
if we're going to protect our country

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.529
in a post-9-11 world.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:50.830
I'm just still shocked

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:51.931
that we don't have control

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.199
of this airspace

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:54.667
from 60,000 to 40,000,

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.669
especially that FAA space

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:57.237
with regard

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:59.072
to what we know is going in there.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.974
David, you have covered the national

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:01.708
security space.

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:02.141
Has the

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.243
when was the last time

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.178
the US scrambled fighter jets

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.846
to shoot something down in U.S.

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:08.114
airspace?

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:10.316
Gee, I can't remember one, Kaitlin.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:10.850
In fact,

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.118
when NORAD's

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:15.154
took down that balloon on Saturday

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:18.825
or what has been described now

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.193
as a balloon.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.161
I think it was the first time that Norway

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.097
had actually fired

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:26.699
in a real live situation, not training

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.868
in North American airspace,

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.137
which which gets to the point

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:32.972
of how unusual this is.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:33.539
But, you know, this

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:34.774
a big distinction

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.843
between the first balloon,

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.811
the one that clearly came from China

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:41.214
and the three that we've seen now

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:42.949
for the first one.

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.917
The US actually tracked it

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:48.655
as it was leaving Hainan Island in China

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:49.522
and saw it

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:51.624
go up over the Aleutians

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.526
and then, of course, warn the president

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.161
and they made the decision

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:56.863
right or wrong, to track it

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.931
across the United States.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.199
These other three,

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.334
there's no indication

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.403
right now that they came from China

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:04.804
Their small size

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:05.405
suggests

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:07.440
that they may have been much more local.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.641
We don't know if they were

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:11.878
foreign powers, balloons at all.

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.413
And so that tells you

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:14.113
that we've sort of got

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:16.783
two separate issues going on here.

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:18.184
The first is

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:20.019
how well we

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:20.887
actually track

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:23.189
these as they come into US airspace.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:24.791
And understand

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:27.126
what the sensitivity of our sensors are.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:27.894
Clearly,

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:28.795
that sensitivity

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.563
has been turned up in recent times.

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:31.364
The way you might

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:33.966
turn up a magnetic reader in an airport.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.468
And then the second is

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:36.669
what are the conditions under

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.071
which you shoot them down?

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.939
And it's not clear right now

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.174
that these posed

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:42.308
these latest balloons

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:43.476
posed a major threat

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:45.511
other than to commercial air traffic.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:46.112
Well, it's interesting

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.880
that a major general on from Norway

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.681
who said, look,

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:51.150
these have been happening for a while now

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:51.417
or that

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.552
maybe it always happened,

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.853
but they've just tweaked the system

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.288
that is able to track them.

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:57.156
My question is, though,

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:57.690
obviously,

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:58.891
the fascination is because it's

00:05:58.891 --> 00:05:59.625
balloons, right?

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:00.927
And it's flying in spaces

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:01.928
with commercial aircraft

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:02.829
that is very dangerous.

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:04.163
But China has said that

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.998
the US has a legally flown, high altitude

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:06.899
balloons into China's

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:07.967
sovereign airspace

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.035
without Beijing's consent

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:11.070
for more than ten times in 20, 22.

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:12.772
We spy on China.

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:14.073
They spy on us.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:16.476
So what gives? What's new here,

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:18.544
Mike Lyons?

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:21.047
Well, I think first and foremost,

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:22.048
we likely do that.

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:23.516
We'd likely put these balloons up there.

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:24.951
We're always looking for an advantage

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:26.686
when it comes to communications.

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:28.621
You know what the balloons provide.

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.123
The military is kind of

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:30.890
skipping off

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:31.257
this instead

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:32.058
of a satellite

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:34.160
from the Earth's atmosphere.

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:35.995
You get better communications

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:36.496
if you can do this.

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:37.764
So there's no question

00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:39.399
that it doesn't surprise me at all

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:40.366
that we've been doing that.

00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:41.267
It's looking to get

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:43.569
an advantage on our side.

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:44.504
Whether they're spy

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:45.805
balloons really remains to be seen

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:47.039
because we have the kind of technology

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:47.907
that could read literally

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:49.976
somebody's nametag in a foxhole down

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:51.911
from space if we had to do that.

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:53.479
So, again,

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:54.580
it's important

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.249
that we're in high altitude.

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:58.217
It's important that we're in that space

00:06:58.217 --> 00:06:59.452
and we can use it to our advantage.

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:01.187
But what does it say to you that they're

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:02.388
they called the first in a balloon?

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.089
As David said,

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:05.158
they're they're not referring to these

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:05.792
as balloons.

00:07:05.792 --> 00:07:07.427
They're referring to them as objects.

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:08.594
So so what are they doing?

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:10.696
Are they emanating pulsing signals?

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:13.833
Are they relaying communications signals?

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:15.034
What exactly is the point?

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:17.470
We don't really know what they are yet.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:18.571
I'm sure the first balloon,

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:19.739
for example, part of the reason

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:20.940
why they are allowed to track it,

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:21.641
because they really wanted

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:22.708
to get inside of it.

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:23.976
It was likely inoculated.

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:25.645
It didn't harm the United States.

00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:26.345
It didn't do anything.

00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:27.280
And they use,

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.714
you know, made a science experiment

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:29.749
out of it, basically,

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:30.516
which is why they convince

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:31.651
the administration to track it

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:32.485
for all that space.

00:07:32.485 --> 00:07:34.654
It seems. It seems that it is.

00:07:34.654 --> 00:07:35.621
David Sanger.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:36.889
More transparency

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:38.524
rather than more incidents. Right.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:39.859
It's like the incidents

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:41.861
you see on cell phones.

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:42.895
They're more cell phones now.

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:44.430
So people are able to to

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.732
to track them more, to see it more.

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:49.635
So this should we be more concerned

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:50.837
about these developments

00:07:50.837 --> 00:07:51.737
or is this good

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:53.072
that we're at least getting more

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:54.006
transparency now?

00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:56.609
Well, Don, you're absolutely right.

00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:56.943
Know, it's

00:07:56.943 --> 00:08:00.313
one of the cardinal rules of intelligence

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:00.580
is that

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.281
if you focus your systems

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:04.317
on looking for a certain kind of thing,

00:08:04.517 --> 00:08:06.018
you're going to find more

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:07.787
because things that sort of

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:09.255
you ignored along the way.

00:08:09.255 --> 00:08:09.589
And I think

00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:11.624
there's a good deal of that happening.

00:08:11.624 --> 00:08:13.960
So we have to fine tune the system now

00:08:14.227 --> 00:08:15.795
to both pick up

00:08:15.795 --> 00:08:17.230
what we really care about.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.532
Not pick up what we don't care about.

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:21.234
And I think probably have a little bit

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:22.235
better sense

00:08:22.235 --> 00:08:23.536
of what we really need to go

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:24.270
shoot down

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.171
because these are

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:27.273
is a pretty dramatic weekend

00:08:27.273 --> 00:08:31.310
Super Bowl aside of of the shoot downs.

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.579
Should we be more concerned?

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:37.216
I think that if we're right to focus

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:37.817
right now

00:08:37.817 --> 00:08:38.584
more on this,

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:40.353
because the Chinese government

00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:42.255
clearly has put together

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:45.224
a very comprehensive surveillance

00:08:45.224 --> 00:08:47.059
system of which the balloons are

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:48.528
just a small part.

00:08:48.528 --> 00:08:49.495
But I'm not sure we should

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:50.663
necessarily panic

00:08:50.663 --> 00:08:52.098
about the smaller incidents.

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:54.667
Big questions still remaining about it,

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:55.034
but No.

00:08:55.034 --> 00:08:56.202
Two better to people

00:08:56.202 --> 00:08:58.070
to speak about it with David Sanger.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.572
Major Mike Lyons, thank you both.

00:08:59.572 --> 00:09:00.339
Good to see both of you.

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:01.307
Thank you very much.

